        "original_id": "ecac29f2-956e-544e-a7db-98f9088ddaaf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Hiwassee, North Carolina; Swain County; Graham County; Cherokee County; North Carolina; United States\n- Structures: Hiwassee Dam; Fontana Dam; Watauga Dam; Hiwassee Reservoir\n- Organizations: Tennessee Valley Authority\n- Water bodies: Little Tennessee River; Hiwassee River\n\nFacts:\n- Fontana Dam is a hydroelectric dam on the Little Tennessee River in Swain and Graham counties, North Carolina, United States.\n- Hiwassee Dam is 307 feet tall and is the third highest dam in the Tennessee Valley Authority system, behind Fontana Dam and Watauga Dam.\n- Hiwassee is a small village in Cherokee County, North Carolina.\n- Hiwassee sits next to Hiwassee Dam and the artificially created Hiwassee Reservoir on the Hiwassee River.",
